  "item_id": "e351f88c9bbc63c033f1aab7",
  "version_id": "de7f1e6f75069d6e82b0732ba9729ef01809dd0621fa585ccb3cb1690c97dcc9",
  "synopsis": "Accepted for piece 03 as researcher guidance on making research inspectable: preserve provenance, share variable descriptions and analysis code, and budget time for planning and methodological review. Applying these practices to delegated computational experiments is an editorial inference. The September 23 podcast contributes a researcher perspective, not a demonstration of autonomous execution or an experimental performance result.",
  "limitations_and_counterevidence": "No agent execution logs, controlled comparisons, held-out evaluations, hardware specifications, quantified budgets or independent replication are supplied. Efficiency and research-quality statements are speaker claims, not measured gains. The transcript's earlier description of sharing as not time-consuming must be read alongside explicit advice to allocate extra time; these concern somewhat different activities and do not establish effortless reproducibility. Sharing is qualified by ethics and, elsewhere in the episode, advance consent planning. The first guest discusses her co-authored report, presented in June; September publication is only anticipated, and neither the original report nor an accessible report link is supplied. The second guest is introduced as editor-in-chief of the journal she recommends. These professional interests limit independence without invalidating the methodological advice. Automatic transcription remains provisional; no audio was checked and uncertain wording has not been repaired. The passages below are citation anchors; this orientation is not a substitute for passage-level support.",
  "passages": [
    {
      "purpose": "Provenance recommendation from the first guest's discussion of her report; read together with adjacent s00292 to complete the recommendation. This is methodological advice, not a tested intervention.",
      "locator": {
        "type": "segment",
        "segment_id": "s00291"
      }
    },
    {
      "purpose": "Adjacent completion of s00291: connects data to its provenance. Supports an attributed recommendation for traceability, not evidence that an agent preserved provenance successfully.",
      "locator": {
        "type": "segment",
        "segment_id": "s00292"
      }
    },
    {
      "purpose": "Ethical qualification on normalizing sharing. Retain this condition when discussing openness; it does not authorize indiscriminate release of research data.",
      "locator": {
        "type": "segment",
        "segment_id": "s00748"
      }
    },
    {
      "purpose": "Concrete inspectability practice: sharing descriptions of variables. Supports guidance about documentation, not demonstrated reproducibility.",
      "locator": {
        "type": "segment",
        "segment_id": "s00799"
      }
    },
    {
      "purpose": "Concrete computational practice: sharing code from a program that was run. Read with adjacent s00802 for the named programming languages; the episode supplies advice rather than the code or execution artifacts themselves.",
      "locator": {
        "type": "segment",
        "segment_id": "s00801"
      }
    },
    {
      "purpose": "Adjacent completion of s00801 naming R and Python as examples. Does not establish that any supplied program was executed or independently reproduced.",
      "locator": {
        "type": "segment",
        "segment_id": "s00802"
      }
    },
    {
      "purpose": "Preserve the earlier characterization of routine sharing as not time-consuming. Pair with s01090's explicit extra-time advice; do not turn this statement into a general cost or effort claim.",
      "locator": {
        "type": "segment",
        "segment_id": "s00752"
      }
    },
    {
      "purpose": "Human time cost and qualification: explicitly recommends building extra time into planning. Counters an effortless-reproducibility reading of s00752 without providing a quantified budget.",
      "locator": {
        "type": "segment",
        "segment_id": "s01090"
      }
    },
    {
      "purpose": "Human methodological gate: in the registered-report explanation, plans are peer reviewed before data collection. Supports guidance about review timing, not proof of better outcomes or fully autonomous discovery.",
      "locator": {
        "type": "segment",
        "segment_id": "s01098"
      }
    },
    {
      "purpose": "Publication-status limitation: the host anticipates September publication of the referenced report. This cannot establish that publication occurred or substitute for inspecting its methods and findings.",
      "locator": {
        "type": "segment",
        "segment_id": "s00568"
      }
    }
  ]
}
